WEBVTT

00:07:58.917 --> 00:08:00.518
We can put that one in too.

00:08:00.542 --> 00:08:01.809
AG: But you're right.

00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:03.893
And I want to become less of a simplifier.

00:08:03.917 --> 00:08:05.684
So let me try to complicate and say,

00:08:05.708 --> 00:08:08.434
when I think about power
from a psychological perspective,

00:08:08.458 --> 00:08:11.184
I think about it also
in terms of influence,

00:08:11.208 --> 00:08:13.226
which is about control over resources.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.393
So one of the reasons
that a CEO is powerful

00:08:15.417 --> 00:08:17.226
is the CEO has control over resources

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:20.601
that lots of people at lower levels
of the organization value and want.

00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:21.893
EP: Correct, correct.

00:08:21.917 --> 00:08:24.934
AG: And so, yeah, I would say
the CEO is dependent in some ways,

00:08:24.958 --> 00:08:27.851
but that the resource control net
outweighs the dependencies.

00:08:27.875 --> 00:08:29.809
And so the CEO is still powerful.

00:08:29.833 --> 00:08:31.268
When you think about these --